<article class="prose-izumi"><p class="eyebrow">Companion</p><h1>Sources & playback</h1><p class="lede">Companion is a TV client, not a catalogue or source provider. It asks your paired izumi client or private Worker for the sources you have configured.</p>
<h2>Supported source paths</h2><div class="table"><div><b>HTTP / HLS / DASH</b><span>Direct web streams are handed to Samsung AVPlay when their format is supported by the TV.</span></div><div><b>Stremio add-ons</b><span>Enable add-ons in izumi. Their stream results are resolved, ranked, and sent to the TV.</span></div><div><b>Debrid</b><span>Configure a supported debrid provider in izumi to turn torrent results into cached HTTP streams.</span></div><div><b>Direct P2P</b><span>Raw torrent playback uses izumi’s native torrent engine and normally requires izumi to remain open.</span></div></div>
<h2>Cloudflare setup</h2><p>The optional private Worker lets the TV request catalog metadata, source results, and configured debrid resolution while izumi is closed. The Worker handles discovery and coordination; media still travels directly to your TV. Device-only, raw P2P, and unusual header-bound sources may still need izumi open.</p>
<h2>Why a source may not play</h2><p>A source can be valid but incompatible with Samsung AVPlay because of its container, codec, subtitles, DRM, headers, or adaptive-streaming profile. Try another result, enable debrid caching, or use izumi as the playback device.</p><p class="next"><a href="/docs/companion/p2p">Next: P2P explained →</a></p></article>
